{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:51.604559Z","id":"1ad588768f02e66c161fb2084ea33b3c0d171b0a1a2a9681eb358458286c1d7d","body":{"detail":"The Ordering section (content/mod.rs:62-83) removes version n when the recording transaction fails. Store::snapshot_pending (store/live.rs:669-701) fails that transaction on purpose (NONE_PENDING) whenever the named threads stopped being pending between its precheck and the transaction, so a git backend would push v<n> and then rewind main. A rewind that is not compare-and-swap on the ref (expected old value v<n>) would discard a commit another writer (another Durable Object, a second process) put on main after v<n>; the in-process ArtifactLocks only serialise writers inside one Store. The compensating step is needed even in a single-threaded Durable Object: the transaction can still fail through `then` (NONE_PENDING), constraint or audit errors, or a full database.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":218},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"5224870b7b553c8bdefd1c11e48e441f1de1d7054cbd29e5d7a7f05ac500416f"},"suggested_fix":"State in remove_version's contract that it removes n only while n is the tip this writer made (a conditional ref update in git), and check the pending condition of snapshot_pending before the content write where it can be checked there, so the common no-op does not push and rewind.","summary":"remove_version as a compensating action means rewinding main and deleting a tag in a git backend; the trait does not require that rewind to be conditional, and live snapshots take it on a routine path","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:51.605231Z","id":"cc0852f8c2633202877fd8a139752a7a2242ad7c340b52b9e5462b20be3cbf00","body":{"detail":"A git backend could write version n's objects unreferenced (content-addressed, so a write is idempotent and a failed transaction leaves only garbage), have the version row record the commit or tree SHA, and read by that SHA; tags and main would then be advanced after the transaction commits, best effort and re-derivable from the rows. That removes remove_version from the write path, the stray-version state that blocks the next write of n (content/mod.rs Ordering: 'block the next write of n until removed'), and the cross-process AlreadyExists race of record 2b832d19. It costs a column on versions and a backend that can read by object ID. Not taken here: FsContent has no content address and this change keeps the on-disk layout unchanged.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"387ae68406f7e8ef4c1ee03b3c18197af337590a36a6912c78505747770ed724"},"summary":"Rows record a content address and refs follow commits, instead of create-only tags with a compensating remove","tags":["content-store","review","revisit:when the Cloudflare Artifacts backend is written, or a second process writes versions","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:51.605539Z","id":"649202fcf418cf5d1876080d53ec8e4eb3e06cf9b53616ff4ca75ddbfaff4622","body":{"detail":"Hosted Clax needs forks. Through this trait a fork is one copy_version per version, and copy_version's default reads and rewrites every file; a git backend can fork a repository natively (the module docs say a whole artifact's history copies with a repository fork, content/mod.rs:47-48, but no method exposes it). No Store operation forks today, so a method added now would have no caller to test it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":186},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"7b7d171d2f7cd2ae5190b052d4a25930c7acc48289deef84185719fc36bf70bb"},"summary":"A fork operation (an artifact's whole history copied into a new artifact) is not in ContentStore","tags":["content-store","review","revisit:when a Store operation copies an artifact's whole history","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:51.605688Z","id":"488499ae833c12a4281f9c334d83fa84d610d0a0ef79600da94fe695ed85d074","body":{"detail":"write_version fails only when n is present or a carried path is missing from n - 1; with no carried paths FsContent and MemContent accept any n. Rows can name a version with no content (an empty files_json version 1, as the store/plans.rs:63 fixture inserts, or a home whose version directory was lost), and copy_version targets numbers past the page's own history. contract.rs never writes n without n - 1 except n = 1, so a git implementation that refuses it would pass the contract and fail in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":174},"end":{"line":179},"content_hash":"439be2827603340578730eb6385f3c61353606f7b10d28589b3bfd40b29dd7d0"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: write_version needs n - 1 only when it carries from it (git roots the commit elsewhere otherwise), and add a contract check that writes version 3 over an absent version 2.","summary":"The contract does not say whether version n may be written when version n - 1 is absent, which a git backend (parent of v<n> is v<n-1>) has to decide","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:51.605842Z","id":"87d077e5a66f749c9938bdf15dc455fbc5d3b49ff9a4919ba239de2cde1bd508","body":{"detail":"Every caller today passes a path recorded in a version's files_json, which publish::check_path (publish.rs:106) validated, or the version's files to carry or copy, so traversal is no easier than before ContentStore. But the trait is public and Store::content() (store/mod.rs:267) hands it out: routes/content.rs already calls read_file on it directly, after a file_meta lookup. A future caller that skips the row lookup would read outside the home with '..' or an absolute path.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"d9f2608b432566b20b5e087c126d5d8f660ddd3b06ec453ede04283450cbbb97"},"suggested_fix":"Return None (reads) or Invalid (writes) from FsContent for a path publish::check_path refuses.","summary":"FsContent joins the paths it is given under the version directory without checking them","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.452569Z","id":"3378278ddea96a9a0a6554fce03bcfd3768f5c393694bd01dbb5979dcab7d1ea","body":{"detail":"The Ordering section (content/mod.rs:62-83) removes version n when the recording transaction fails. Store::snapshot_pending (store/live.rs:669-701) fails that transaction on purpose (NONE_PENDING) whenever the named threads stopped being pending between its precheck and the transaction, so a git backend would push v<n> and then rewind main. A rewind that is not compare-and-swap on the ref (expected old value v<n>) would discard a commit another writer (another Durable Object, a second process) put on main after v<n>; the in-process ArtifactLocks only serialise writers inside one Store. The compensating step is needed even in a single-threaded Durable Object: the transaction can still fail through `then` (NONE_PENDING), constraint or audit errors, or a full database.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"5224870b7b553c8bdefd1c11e48e441f1de1d7054cbd29e5d7a7f05ac500416f"},"suggested_fix":"State in remove_version's contract that it removes n only while n is the tip this writer made (a conditional ref update in git), and check the pending condition of snapshot_pending before the content write where it can be checked there, so the common no-op does not push and rewind.","summary":"remove_version as a compensating action means rewinding main and deleting a tag in a git backend; the trait does not require that rewind to be conditional, and live snapshots take it on a routine path","supersedes":"1ad588768f02e66c161fb2084ea33b3c0d171b0a1a2a9681eb358458286c1d7d","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.458030Z","id":"78e488f7a07d381018aa5fda24faffad0c04c9653348b48982243164ac4eac38","body":{"detail":"Hosted Clax needs forks. Through this trait a fork is one copy_version per version, and copy_version's default reads and rewrites every file; a git backend can fork a repository natively (the module docs say a whole artifact's history copies with a repository fork, content/mod.rs:47-48, but no method exposes it). No Store operation forks today, so a method added now would have no caller to test it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":174},"end":{"line":194},"content_hash":"7b7d171d2f7cd2ae5190b052d4a25930c7acc48289deef84185719fc36bf70bb"},"summary":"A fork operation (an artifact's whole history copied into a new artifact) is not in ContentStore","supersedes":"649202fcf418cf5d1876080d53ec8e4eb3e06cf9b53616ff4ca75ddbfaff4622","tags":["content-store","review","revisit:when a Store operation copies an artifact's whole history","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.462900Z","id":"b73ad868867b2c5c336544204e4b3b3e3dad6f04a3d5b44e2225ef31e8cb5322","body":{"detail":"write_version fails only when n is present or a carried path is missing from n - 1; with no carried paths FsContent and MemContent accept any n. Rows can name a version with no content (an empty files_json version 1, as the store/plans.rs:63 fixture inserts, or a home whose version directory was lost), and copy_version targets numbers past the page's own history. contract.rs never writes n without n - 1 except n = 1, so a git implementation that refuses it would pass the contract and fail in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"439be2827603340578730eb6385f3c61353606f7b10d28589b3bfd40b29dd7d0"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: write_version needs n - 1 only when it carries from it (git roots the commit elsewhere otherwise), and add a contract check that writes version 3 over an absent version 2.","summary":"The contract does not say whether version n may be written when version n - 1 is absent, which a git backend (parent of v<n> is v<n-1>) has to decide","supersedes":"488499ae833c12a4281f9c334d83fa84d610d0a0ef79600da94fe695ed85d074","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.459902Z","id":"7971bec64cea64ab2c851301e44a9d6ef76cced0aec52a68d3531e9c97db08e2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8326eb9d","summary":"Fixed: remove_version is conditional on the tip. The contract (content/mod.rs Versions) removes only the newest version, and in git a remove is one atomic compare-and-swap that deletes v<n> only while it names the commit read and moves main back only while main is at it (crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs remove_version); with main moved past, it fails and leaves both. `cargo test -p clax-content-git races::`: 7 passed, including a_remove_never_discards_a_commit_another_writer_put_on_top and a_remove_is_refused_when_main_holds_a_pushed_commit_on_top","supersedes":"1ad588768f02e66c161fb2084ea33b3c0d171b0a1a2a9681eb358458286c1d7d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.465710Z","id":"3f1bfecec2cba4945f361257b38dfa8b5744d0ff6a8949a1d6acd8ebfc6b4966","body":{"detail":"Each write and remove is one atomic Repo::apply whose old values are the refs as read (receive-pack's old-value check over smart HTTP), so the compensating remove can never discard another writer's commit (record 1ad58876, closed by git:8326eb9d), and the filesystem and git stores keep one contract with no new versions column. What this alternative would still remove: the stray unrecorded version that blocks the next write of n until removed, and the routine remove after Store::snapshot_pending's NONE_PENDING. Its revisit trigger stays as written for the second-process case.","kind":"comment","references":"cc0852f8c2633202877fd8a139752a7a2242ad7c340b52b9e5462b20be3cbf00","summary":"Not taken in the git backend either: crates/clax-content-git keeps create-only tags with a compensating remove, made safe by compare and swap","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.465975Z","id":"a2497a85dc479579b13269d079537b376dfd789fd804c90a3031666cf27ec028","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a0ccd44f","summary":"Fixed: the contract says what version n follows. content/mod.rs Versions: n follows the newest present version below it (none for a first version, which may be any number); carried paths come from n - 1 only; a write or remove of n fails while a version above n is present. FsContent and MemContent enforce it; GitContent parents v<n> on that version's commit. `cargo test -p clax-core --lib content::` 8 passed and `cargo test -p clax-content-git contract::` 3 passed, both running contract::versions_are_written_in_order_and_only_the_newest_is_removed","supersedes":"488499ae833c12a4281f9c334d83fa84d610d0a0ef79600da94fe695ed85d074","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.469290Z","id":"bfe3ac8e97a48c1316b4ebf361430122e5e199880947d5ad26b1a7acb5bc7ed6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a0ccd44f","summary":"Fixed: ContentStore::fork(from, from_n, paths, to) makes version 1 of a new artifact; the default copies (FsContent, MemContent), GitContent forks the repository with its history. Hosted Clax forks artifacts (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts fork and initFork). No Store operation calls it yet. Contract check contract::a_fork_makes_version_one_of_a_new_artifact passes for all three: `cargo test -p clax-core --lib content::` 8 passed, `cargo test -p clax-content-git contract::` 3 passed","supersedes":"649202fcf418cf5d1876080d53ec8e4eb3e06cf9b53616ff4ca75ddbfaff4622","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:05:54.477603Z","id":"9cbeae2fe05734af3c59ad98b337464c240242b902f3b2059785c9d22f4d3348","body":{"detail":"A git backend could write version n's objects unreferenced (content-addressed, so a write is idempotent and a failed transaction leaves only garbage), have the version row record the commit or tree SHA, and read by that SHA; tags and main would then be advanced after the transaction commits, best effort and re-derivable from the rows. That removes remove_version from the write path, the stray-version state that blocks the next write of n (content/mod.rs Ordering: 'block the next write of n until removed'), and the cross-process AlreadyExists race of record 2b832d19. It costs a column on versions and a backend that can read by object ID. Not taken here: FsContent has no content address and this change keeps the on-disk layout unchanged.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"8dfbd5460db09bfae2052cb741434eba608cb27b44722a250b298a1ec3c03424"},"summary":"Rows record a content address and refs follow commits, instead of create-only tags with a compensating remove","supersedes":"cc0852f8c2633202877fd8a139752a7a2242ad7c340b52b9e5462b20be3cbf00","tags":["content-store","review","revisit:when the Cloudflare Artifacts backend is written, or a second process writes versions","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.830741Z","id":"cbc6b60ebf85a0b346af70247b0e096a820fb4b6cf4c97dba23b6d0fa7553b8a","body":{"detail":"A git backend could write version n's objects unreferenced (content-addressed, so a write is idempotent and a failed transaction leaves only garbage), have the version row record the commit or tree SHA, and read by that SHA; tags and main would then be advanced after the transaction commits, best effort and re-derivable from the rows. That removes remove_version from the write path, the stray-version state that blocks the next write of n (content/mod.rs Ordering: 'block the next write of n until removed'), and the cross-process AlreadyExists race of record 2b832d19. It costs a column on versions and a backend that can read by object ID. Not taken here: FsContent has no content address and this change keeps the on-disk layout unchanged.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"0019a9daf1aac537495280ca1095fec1c97dab914abef612479cf30fb117d797"},"summary":"Rows record a content address and refs follow commits, instead of create-only tags with a compensating remove","supersedes":"9cbeae2fe05734af3c59ad98b337464c240242b902f3b2059785c9d22f4d3348","tags":["content-store","review","revisit:when the Cloudflare Artifacts backend is written, or a second process writes versions","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.836625Z","id":"a7763cba3919637d4ca1edca5b3c85fafeda2431bb73033cad6c1f3424120ed0","body":{"detail":"FsContent::write_version refuses n while any version directory above n holds index.html (above, check_new). Before, a stray above current_version + 1 was harmless until the artifact reached its number; now publishing stops at once with 'version m of <id>, newer than version n, is present' (an I/O error, not Conflict). Strays above current + 1 without current + 1 itself come only from a failed remove_version (logged) after re-filing placed several versions, which before site.rs remove_placed went newest-first removed the oldest first, or from hand edits; clax doctor lists them as stale_files and --fix removes them (commands/doctor.rs stale_files, apply_fixes). No migration renumbers versions or lowers current_version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"cc38183f7027ded45616a826ad0482bd6f1b550f755e16637ffa9007a2ac5132"},"suggested_fix":"Have the store name the stray in its error and point at clax doctor --fix, or let FsContent ignore versions above n that no row records (it cannot see rows, so the store would pass current_version).","summary":"A stray version directory above n+1 now blocks every publish of the artifact, where before it blocked only the write of its own number","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:31.535436Z","id":"a389f3e2b2311330a8d8724449541718a5b1daa36d7a509462dc0bc7091c7e06","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks::held records std::thread::current() when the lock is taken, and Store::lock_content refuses (WouldBlock) a synchronous method on the thread recorded. A future polled by a multi-threaded executor that takes the lock on thread A and resumes on B leaves A recorded: a synchronous method on A is refused although it would not deadlock, and one on B waits for a lock its own thread now drives. Neither happens today (the server drives only synchronous methods, on store workers; a Worker has one thread).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":413},"end":{"line":428},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"A content lock's holder is the thread it was taken on, so a future that moves threads after taking it is misattributed","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.660662Z","id":"27e7b8764246d79c9e5d43c91688dc2d3b2efa693eaa4ff13ff5c0caeef56008","body":{"detail":"Every caller today passes a path recorded in a version's files_json, which publish::check_path (publish.rs:106) validated, or the version's files to carry or copy, so traversal is no easier than before ContentStore. But the trait is public and Store::content() (store/mod.rs:267) hands it out: routes/content.rs already calls read_file on it directly, after a file_meta lookup. A future caller that skips the row lookup would read outside the home with '..' or an absolute path.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"d9f2608b432566b20b5e087c126d5d8f660ddd3b06ec453ede04283450cbbb97"},"suggested_fix":"Return None (reads) or Invalid (writes) from FsContent for a path publish::check_path refuses.","summary":"FsContent joins the paths it is given under the version directory without checking them","supersedes":"87d077e5a66f749c9938bdf15dc455fbc5d3b49ff9a4919ba239de2cde1bd508","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.672765Z","id":"4c505c2d4495745f0c676cb761dd5faf383c96e5d62cf8456a38872369024ad9","body":{"detail":"write_version fails only when n is present or a carried path is missing from n - 1; with no carried paths FsContent and MemContent accept any n. Rows can name a version with no content (an empty files_json version 1, as the store/plans.rs:63 fixture inserts, or a home whose version directory was lost), and copy_version targets numbers past the page's own history. contract.rs never writes n without n - 1 except n = 1, so a git implementation that refuses it would pass the contract and fail in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":183},"end":{"line":188},"content_hash":"439be2827603340578730eb6385f3c61353606f7b10d28589b3bfd40b29dd7d0"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: write_version needs n - 1 only when it carries from it (git roots the commit elsewhere otherwise), and add a contract check that writes version 3 over an absent version 2.","summary":"The contract does not say whether version n may be written when version n - 1 is absent, which a git backend (parent of v<n> is v<n-1>) has to decide","supersedes":"488499ae833c12a4281f9c334d83fa84d610d0a0ef79600da94fe695ed85d074","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.675508Z","id":"cf94976c59a5e885288d525fbf0308bf8ce2e61c2c0cbea957550182e853263a","body":{"detail":"Hosted Clax needs forks. Through this trait a fork is one copy_version per version, and copy_version's default reads and rewrites every file; a git backend can fork a repository natively (the module docs say a whole artifact's history copies with a repository fork, content/mod.rs:47-48, but no method exposes it). No Store operation forks today, so a method added now would have no caller to test it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":195},"end":{"line":215},"content_hash":"7b7d171d2f7cd2ae5190b052d4a25930c7acc48289deef84185719fc36bf70bb"},"summary":"A fork operation (an artifact's whole history copied into a new artifact) is not in ContentStore","supersedes":"649202fcf418cf5d1876080d53ec8e4eb3e06cf9b53616ff4ca75ddbfaff4622","tags":["content-store","review","revisit:when a Store operation copies an artifact's whole history","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.689437Z","id":"ef835be917547910d4d71a036dab7f1940abd9281e1528a488f85388eebd64a8","body":{"detail":"The Ordering section (content/mod.rs:62-83) removes version n when the recording transaction fails. Store::snapshot_pending (store/live.rs:669-701) fails that transaction on purpose (NONE_PENDING) whenever the named threads stopped being pending between its precheck and the transaction, so a git backend would push v<n> and then rewind main. A rewind that is not compare-and-swap on the ref (expected old value v<n>) would discard a commit another writer (another Durable Object, a second process) put on main after v<n>; the in-process ArtifactLocks only serialise writers inside one Store. The compensating step is needed even in a single-threaded Durable Object: the transaction can still fail through `then` (NONE_PENDING), constraint or audit errors, or a full database.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":227},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"5224870b7b553c8bdefd1c11e48e441f1de1d7054cbd29e5d7a7f05ac500416f"},"suggested_fix":"State in remove_version's contract that it removes n only while n is the tip this writer made (a conditional ref update in git), and check the pending condition of snapshot_pending before the content write where it can be checked there, so the common no-op does not push and rewind.","summary":"remove_version as a compensating action means rewinding main and deleting a tag in a git backend; the trait does not require that rewind to be conditional, and live snapshots take it on a routine path","supersedes":"1ad588768f02e66c161fb2084ea33b3c0d171b0a1a2a9681eb358458286c1d7d","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.337879Z","id":"223ec0dc9e6e80516af51ba25dd6ffa1d13326b7798f915ea26dfadebcf55204","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks::held records std::thread::current() when the lock is taken, and Store::lock_content refuses (WouldBlock) a synchronous method on the thread recorded. A future polled by a multi-threaded executor that takes the lock on thread A and resumes on B leaves A recorded: a synchronous method on A is refused although it would not deadlock, and one on B waits for a lock its own thread now drives. Neither happens today (the server drives only synchronous methods, on store workers; a Worker has one thread).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":474},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"A content lock's holder is the thread it was taken on, so a future that moves threads after taking it is misattributed","supersedes":"a389f3e2b2311330a8d8724449541718a5b1daa36d7a509462dc0bc7091c7e06","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.363856Z","id":"a9c5f783a767fbe813e80e758cd7532263acbc133ad512a33c2c61b6b3a906c5","body":{"detail":"The trait (content/mod.rs, local_file) promises the file that holds the bytes; FsContent returns the computed path unconditionally. Callers gate on has_clip and recorded versions (store/feedback.rs, clax-server feedback.rs views_and_senders), so the path is right unless the home lost the file, in which case an agent is handed a path that does not exist. Same as before 274f3832 (the home paths were computed the same way).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":223},"end":{"line":229},"content_hash":"83c1b1a583691ffd80d5b7e68589cfbc92d491645be3ce6763b7522a0eba362b"},"summary":"FsContent::local_file and local_clip answer a path whether or not the file is there","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:53.498205Z","id":"953e679a9ec4120f6b5dbd751458f283867ac7e1b574aab346e52a384cbc3d50","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"223ec0dc9e6e80516af51ba25dd6ffa1d13326b7798f915ea26dfadebcf55204","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":474},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"Since 5d7572d1 the server awaits async twins inline on its request task when the store is on one connection (Store::call_async, store/exec.rs:910), so a lock taken by a future on one tokio worker and resumed on another can now happen natively, but only on a store opened with Store::open_on on a multi-threaded runtime (tests: TestServer::spawn_on_one_connection, CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred). The daemon pool still drives every content job through Store::block_on on a store worker, where the holder thread is exact; a Durable Object has one thread.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.013249Z","id":"463feef64b8fb886f5e8f4a9afd473c0dce42b616286460c4502f8a76ef5900b","body":{"detail":"The Ordering section (content/mod.rs:62-83) removes version n when the recording transaction fails. Store::snapshot_pending (store/live.rs:669-701) fails that transaction on purpose (NONE_PENDING) whenever the named threads stopped being pending between its precheck and the transaction, so a git backend would push v<n> and then rewind main. A rewind that is not compare-and-swap on the ref (expected old value v<n>) would discard a commit another writer (another Durable Object, a second process) put on main after v<n>; the in-process ArtifactLocks only serialise writers inside one Store. The compensating step is needed even in a single-threaded Durable Object: the transaction can still fail through `then` (NONE_PENDING), constraint or audit errors, or a full database.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":216},"end":{"line":216},"content_hash":"5224870b7b553c8bdefd1c11e48e441f1de1d7054cbd29e5d7a7f05ac500416f"},"suggested_fix":"State in remove_version's contract that it removes n only while n is the tip this writer made (a conditional ref update in git), and check the pending condition of snapshot_pending before the content write where it can be checked there, so the common no-op does not push and rewind.","summary":"remove_version as a compensating action means rewinding main and deleting a tag in a git backend; the trait does not require that rewind to be conditional, and live snapshots take it on a routine path","supersedes":"3378278ddea96a9a0a6554fce03bcfd3768f5c393694bd01dbb5979dcab7d1ea","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.020393Z","id":"3599cd6602c70575a756ee048a0466d2d684361b16e8d4eece3d8c1251e01a3d","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 3378278ddea96a9a0a6554fce03bcfd3768f5c393694bd01dbb5979dcab7d1ea, the other head of the same record (both supersede 1ad588768f02e66c161fb2084ea33b3c0d171b0a1a2a9681eb358458286c1d7d); that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs:216:216.","supersedes":"ef835be917547910d4d71a036dab7f1940abd9281e1528a488f85388eebd64a8","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
