{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.027634Z","id":"5c60c2f6bf21ff62e72be3bbc2d1c2ef24a5037767e7bbf026f24ef879053b32","body":{"detail":"write_version fails only when n is present or a carried path is missing from n - 1; with no carried paths FsContent and MemContent accept any n. Rows can name a version with no content (an empty files_json version 1, as the store/plans.rs:63 fixture inserts, or a home whose version directory was lost), and copy_version targets numbers past the page's own history. contract.rs never writes n without n - 1 except n = 1, so a git implementation that refuses it would pass the contract and fail in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":177},"content_hash":"439be2827603340578730eb6385f3c61353606f7b10d28589b3bfd40b29dd7d0"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: write_version needs n - 1 only when it carries from it (git roots the commit elsewhere otherwise), and add a contract check that writes version 3 over an absent version 2.","summary":"The contract does not say whether version n may be written when version n - 1 is absent, which a git backend (parent of v<n> is v<n-1>) has to decide","supersedes":"b73ad868867b2c5c336544204e4b3b3e3dad6f04a3d5b44e2225ef31e8cb5322","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.029691Z","id":"6a921b986f2084fcfee383b1b18d29f52893423bb3eee675dd4f5539058b397c","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of b73ad868867b2c5c336544204e4b3b3e3dad6f04a3d5b44e2225ef31e8cb5322, the other head of the same record (both supersede 488499ae833c12a4281f9c334d83fa84d610d0a0ef79600da94fe695ed85d074); that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs:172:177.","supersedes":"4c505c2d4495745f0c676cb761dd5faf383c96e5d62cf8456a38872369024ad9","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.031832Z","id":"a04abe565f961ea22c28b45c9aad95a0ec4b7cabbb4c8639a3ad04a8e3b1f2c2","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks::held records std::thread::current() when the lock is taken, and Store::lock_content refuses (WouldBlock) a synchronous method on the thread recorded. A future polled by a multi-threaded executor that takes the lock on thread A and resumes on B leaves A recorded: a synchronous method on A is refused although it would not deadlock, and one on B waits for a lock its own thread now drives. Neither happens today (the server drives only synchronous methods, on store workers; a Worker has one thread).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":463},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"A content lock's holder is the thread it was taken on, so a future that moves threads after taking it is misattributed","supersedes":"223ec0dc9e6e80516af51ba25dd6ffa1d13326b7798f915ea26dfadebcf55204","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:58.460956Z","id":"fa8b4ce6281fe629044b9127da8aebd3d41a85461e99f939368f6e0bebff76b2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a04abe565f961ea22c28b45c9aad95a0ec4b7cabbb4c8639a3ad04a8e3b1f2c2","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":463},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"Since 5d7572d1 the server awaits async twins inline on its request task when the store is on one connection (Store::call_async, store/exec.rs:910), so a lock taken by a future on one tokio worker and resumed on another can now happen natively, but only on a store opened with Store::open_on on a multi-threaded runtime (tests: TestServer::spawn_on_one_connection, CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred). The daemon pool still drives every content job through Store::block_on on a store worker, where the holder thread is exact; a Durable Object has one thread.","supersedes":"953e679a9ec4120f6b5dbd751458f283867ac7e1b574aab346e52a384cbc3d50","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.539625Z","id":"c70b5f8062599f6941a43a53f05a7d9fe9b5042ad7eeebb5903813af99265900","body":{"detail":"FsContent::write_version refuses n while any version directory above n holds index.html (above, check_new). Before, a stray above current_version + 1 was harmless until the artifact reached its number; now publishing stops at once with 'version m of <id>, newer than version n, is present' (an I/O error, not Conflict). Strays above current + 1 without current + 1 itself come only from a failed remove_version (logged) after re-filing placed several versions, which before site.rs remove_placed went newest-first removed the oldest first, or from hand edits; clax doctor lists them as stale_files and --fix removes them (commands/doctor.rs stale_files, apply_fixes). No migration renumbers versions or lowers current_version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":123},"content_hash":"cc38183f7027ded45616a826ad0482bd6f1b550f755e16637ffa9007a2ac5132"},"suggested_fix":"Have the store name the stray in its error and point at clax doctor --fix, or let FsContent ignore versions above n that no row records (it cannot see rows, so the store would pass current_version).","summary":"A stray version directory above n+1 now blocks every publish of the artifact, where before it blocked only the write of its own number","supersedes":"a7763cba3919637d4ca1edca5b3c85fafeda2431bb73033cad6c1f3424120ed0","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.553577Z","id":"666847316c6b86150e8ec4a1ac226b18f5b63f3f9cc48d1bb639af8b644d4760","body":{"detail":"The trait (content/mod.rs, local_file) promises the file that holds the bytes; FsContent returns the computed path unconditionally. Callers gate on has_clip and recorded versions (store/feedback.rs, clax-server feedback.rs views_and_senders), so the path is right unless the home lost the file, in which case an agent is handed a path that does not exist. Same as before 274f3832 (the home paths were computed the same way).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"83c1b1a583691ffd80d5b7e68589cfbc92d491645be3ce6763b7522a0eba362b"},"summary":"FsContent::local_file and local_clip answer a path whether or not the file is there","supersedes":"a9c5f783a767fbe813e80e758cd7532263acbc133ad512a33c2c61b6b3a906c5","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.595367Z","id":"f6d8ee8e9b0c419078029965764c5989a99faf7385b5c0df47405d1e46dabdf4","body":{"detail":"The Ordering section (content/mod.rs:62-83) removes version n when the recording transaction fails. Store::snapshot_pending (store/live.rs:669-701) fails that transaction on purpose (NONE_PENDING) whenever the named threads stopped being pending between its precheck and the transaction, so a git backend would push v<n> and then rewind main. A rewind that is not compare-and-swap on the ref (expected old value v<n>) would discard a commit another writer (another Durable Object, a second process) put on main after v<n>; the in-process ArtifactLocks only serialise writers inside one Store. The compensating step is needed even in a single-threaded Durable Object: the transaction can still fail through `then` (NONE_PENDING), constraint or audit errors, or a full database.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":285},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"5224870b7b553c8bdefd1c11e48e441f1de1d7054cbd29e5d7a7f05ac500416f"},"suggested_fix":"State in remove_version's contract that it removes n only while n is the tip this writer made (a conditional ref update in git), and check the pending condition of snapshot_pending before the content write where it can be checked there, so the common no-op does not push and rewind.","summary":"remove_version as a compensating action means rewinding main and deleting a tag in a git backend; the trait does not require that rewind to be conditional, and live snapshots take it on a routine path","supersedes":"463feef64b8fb886f5e8f4a9afd473c0dce42b616286460c4502f8a76ef5900b","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.608633Z","id":"f752c741defb42e35341864302e10f794aee12ebf8b73a2ed458b4a43a4de109","body":{"detail":"Hosted Clax needs forks. Through this trait a fork is one copy_version per version, and copy_version's default reads and rewrites every file; a git backend can fork a repository natively (the module docs say a whole artifact's history copies with a repository fork, content/mod.rs:47-48, but no method exposes it). No Store operation forks today, so a method added now would have no caller to test it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":233},"end":{"line":253},"content_hash":"7b7d171d2f7cd2ae5190b052d4a25930c7acc48289deef84185719fc36bf70bb"},"summary":"A fork operation (an artifact's whole history copied into a new artifact) is not in ContentStore","supersedes":"046418c8b63dc8fab2a18763cff01ad31620c1ee43cdb7c48ff5852d27fae4ad","tags":["content-store","review","revisit:when a Store operation copies an artifact's whole history","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.636071Z","id":"7c7621d90f896ec178779f1845ef54a11b35d4938cb104beeccabd28ba9c7924","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks::held records std::thread::current() when the lock is taken, and Store::lock_content refuses (WouldBlock) a synchronous method on the thread recorded. A future polled by a multi-threaded executor that takes the lock on thread A and resumes on B leaves A recorded: a synchronous method on A is refused although it would not deadlock, and one on B waits for a lock its own thread now drives. Neither happens today (the server drives only synchronous methods, on store workers; a Worker has one thread).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":526},"end":{"line":541},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"A content lock's holder is the thread it was taken on, so a future that moves threads after taking it is misattributed","supersedes":"a04abe565f961ea22c28b45c9aad95a0ec4b7cabbb4c8639a3ad04a8e3b1f2c2","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.076687Z","id":"1d21d6c17fba34e741ad0d8c34db0cfaa7109f5ee066e794736e81e323519b3c","body":{"detail":"write_version fails only when n is present or a carried path is missing from n - 1; with no carried paths FsContent and MemContent accept any n. Rows can name a version with no content (an empty files_json version 1, as the store/plans.rs:63 fixture inserts, or a home whose version directory was lost), and copy_version targets numbers past the page's own history. contract.rs never writes n without n - 1 except n = 1, so a git implementation that refuses it would pass the contract and fail in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":220},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"490d14f7f42c25621eab7c8f617d19f120b78adae0a6ba4bebf466fdf6214436"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: write_version needs n - 1 only when it carries from it (git roots the commit elsewhere otherwise), and add a contract check that writes version 3 over an absent version 2.","summary":"The contract does not say whether version n may be written when version n - 1 is absent, which a git backend (parent of v<n> is v<n-1>) has to decide","supersedes":"5c60c2f6bf21ff62e72be3bbc2d1c2ef24a5037767e7bbf026f24ef879053b32","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:51.114315Z","id":"ee85ced8db55cfea5e7fb8e2b47969bc0789a9e3682503945dc7d0a4e5b2e22c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7c7621d90f896ec178779f1845ef54a11b35d4938cb104beeccabd28ba9c7924","span":{"start":{"line":526},"end":{"line":541},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"Since 5d7572d1 the server awaits async twins inline on its request task when the store is on one connection (Store::call_async, store/exec.rs:910), so a lock taken by a future on one tokio worker and resumed on another can now happen natively, but only on a store opened with Store::open_on on a multi-threaded runtime (tests: TestServer::spawn_on_one_connection, CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred). The daemon pool still drives every content job through Store::block_on on a store worker, where the holder thread is exact; a Durable Object has one thread.","supersedes":"fa8b4ce6281fe629044b9127da8aebd3d41a85461e99f939368f6e0bebff76b2","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:35:32.220478Z","id":"3add76e15ec72403a151fd2ac1105cf576e2557b5e8cbbe01acf252a78b613c0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f752c741defb42e35341864302e10f794aee12ebf8b73a2ed458b4a43a4de109","summary":"ContentStore::fork is in the trait (content/mod.rs) and has a Store caller since fc6a2add (Store::fork_artifact_async); this alternative reads as taken and may be closed.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.199214Z","id":"824a0e8e3986ee87d2788cedd346d8627d4ee14b6d3098c923a042ee2bfaa811","body":{"detail":"The Ordering section (content/mod.rs:62-83) removes version n when the recording transaction fails. Store::snapshot_pending (store/live.rs:669-701) fails that transaction on purpose (NONE_PENDING) whenever the named threads stopped being pending between its precheck and the transaction, so a git backend would push v<n> and then rewind main. A rewind that is not compare-and-swap on the ref (expected old value v<n>) would discard a commit another writer (another Durable Object, a second process) put on main after v<n>; the in-process ArtifactLocks only serialise writers inside one Store. The compensating step is needed even in a single-threaded Durable Object: the transaction can still fail through `then` (NONE_PENDING), constraint or audit errors, or a full database.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":290},"end":{"line":290},"content_hash":"5224870b7b553c8bdefd1c11e48e441f1de1d7054cbd29e5d7a7f05ac500416f"},"suggested_fix":"State in remove_version's contract that it removes n only while n is the tip this writer made (a conditional ref update in git), and check the pending condition of snapshot_pending before the content write where it can be checked there, so the common no-op does not push and rewind.","summary":"remove_version as a compensating action means rewinding main and deleting a tag in a git backend; the trait does not require that rewind to be conditional, and live snapshots take it on a routine path","supersedes":"f6d8ee8e9b0c419078029965764c5989a99faf7385b5c0df47405d1e46dabdf4","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.202638Z","id":"57ab97cd7d1174101dc4bc7bb16dab9379c58b20d1a79eeb05b473c675138887","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks::held records std::thread::current() when the lock is taken, and Store::lock_content refuses (WouldBlock) a synchronous method on the thread recorded. A future polled by a multi-threaded executor that takes the lock on thread A and resumes on B leaves A recorded: a synchronous method on A is refused although it would not deadlock, and one on B waits for a lock its own thread now drives. Neither happens today (the server drives only synchronous methods, on store workers; a Worker has one thread).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":531},"end":{"line":546},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"A content lock's holder is the thread it was taken on, so a future that moves threads after taking it is misattributed","supersedes":"7c7621d90f896ec178779f1845ef54a11b35d4938cb104beeccabd28ba9c7924","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.948270Z","id":"f5b72fcec6abd66f5c8b0acb377ebb9d762d8436d5cc36ea9445399ca96e20ef","body":{"detail":"scripts/check-wasm.sh passes (it checks, not lints); cargo clippy --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p clax-server -- -D warnings fails in clax-core on never_loop (content/mod.rs block_on, whose loop body returns on wasm32) and drop_non_drop (gitctx.rs), so the wasm32 clippy of clax-server passes only with --no-deps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":399},"end":{"line":405},"content_hash":"6b7c2b36baa3004dad1f7399618085267d8135a48cce90ef21b3924de541abd5"},"summary":"cargo clippy --target wasm32-unknown-unknown on clax-core fails: a loop that never loops here, and drop of a ChildStdout at gitctx.rs:865 and :895","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:20:28.281276Z","id":"5dfdf4432ef7f8336e0a9b16b64c1c79b1fd5ce530e39ba95c1263c64d484543","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:160e284a","summary":"never_loop on content::wait and drop_non_drop on gitctx's output and diff are allowed on wasm32 alone, and arc_with_non_send_sync on ClaxTools::new, the one lint behind them in clax-mcp. Evidence: cargo clippy --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p clax-core -p clax-rt -p clax-mcp -p clax-content-git -p clax-server -- -D warnings finishes with no warning, without --no-deps.","supersedes":"f5b72fcec6abd66f5c8b0acb377ebb9d762d8436d5cc36ea9445399ca96e20ef","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:21:25.540910Z","id":"3cf8f5832b606429ced7d1fe876d58c51f03e174c3bd52eea85d4c7224dbf97e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7c7621d90f896ec178779f1845ef54a11b35d4938cb104beeccabd28ba9c7924","span":{"start":{"line":528},"end":{"line":543},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"Since 5d7572d1 the server awaits async twins inline on its request task when the store is on one connection (Store::call_async, store/exec.rs:910), so a lock taken by a future on one tokio worker and resumed on another can now happen natively, but only on a store opened with Store::open_on on a multi-threaded runtime (tests: TestServer::spawn_on_one_connection, CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred). The daemon pool still drives every content job through Store::block_on on a store worker, where the holder thread is exact; a Durable Object has one thread.","supersedes":"ee85ced8db55cfea5e7fb8e2b47969bc0789a9e3682503945dc7d0a4e5b2e22c","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
