{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.321237Z","id":"b93ae0d6ce390925d67c7a5c60a1cdc043bc7ee35bf4b66c03e8525531bd947c","body":{"detail":"The Ordering section (content/mod.rs:62-83) removes version n when the recording transaction fails. Store::snapshot_pending (store/live.rs:669-701) fails that transaction on purpose (NONE_PENDING) whenever the named threads stopped being pending between its precheck and the transaction, so a git backend would push v<n> and then rewind main. A rewind that is not compare-and-swap on the ref (expected old value v<n>) would discard a commit another writer (another Durable Object, a second process) put on main after v<n>; the in-process ArtifactLocks only serialise writers inside one Store. The compensating step is needed even in a single-threaded Durable Object: the transaction can still fail through `then` (NONE_PENDING), constraint or audit errors, or a full database.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":310},"end":{"line":310},"content_hash":"5224870b7b553c8bdefd1c11e48e441f1de1d7054cbd29e5d7a7f05ac500416f"},"suggested_fix":"State in remove_version's contract that it removes n only while n is the tip this writer made (a conditional ref update in git), and check the pending condition of snapshot_pending before the content write where it can be checked there, so the common no-op does not push and rewind.","summary":"remove_version as a compensating action means rewinding main and deleting a tag in a git backend; the trait does not require that rewind to be conditional, and live snapshots take it on a routine path","supersedes":"f6d8ee8e9b0c419078029965764c5989a99faf7385b5c0df47405d1e46dabdf4","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.328372Z","id":"ea0434728d7a141c66b29685b2dadb7011cc0d45c910b28e4f14b9a7b1df46e2","body":{"detail":"Hosted Clax needs forks. Through this trait a fork is one copy_version per version, and copy_version's default reads and rewrites every file; a git backend can fork a repository natively (the module docs say a whole artifact's history copies with a repository fork, content/mod.rs:47-48, but no method exposes it). No Store operation forks today, so a method added now would have no caller to test it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":258},"end":{"line":278},"content_hash":"7b7d171d2f7cd2ae5190b052d4a25930c7acc48289deef84185719fc36bf70bb"},"summary":"A fork operation (an artifact's whole history copied into a new artifact) is not in ContentStore","supersedes":"f752c741defb42e35341864302e10f794aee12ebf8b73a2ed458b4a43a4de109","tags":["content-store","review","revisit:when a Store operation copies an artifact's whole history","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
