{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:34:05.502826Z","id":"cf5bea50d540fa512452c4bb5c986cf6240e277f4436045799563613fedd9cf9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9983982150bdbba29a4cd231e43d749a8f060dbda2a3f1d104d4f88108d8ddd2","span":{"start":{"line":687},"end":{"line":702},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"Since 5d7572d1 the server awaits async twins inline on its request task when the store is on one connection (Store::call_async, store/exec.rs:910), so a lock taken by a future on one tokio worker and resumed on another can now happen natively, but only on a store opened with Store::open_on on a multi-threaded runtime (tests: TestServer::spawn_on_one_connection, CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred). The daemon pool still drives every content job through Store::block_on on a store worker, where the holder thread is exact; a Durable Object has one thread.","supersedes":"ee85ced8db55cfea5e7fb8e2b47969bc0789a9e3682503945dc7d0a4e5b2e22c","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
