{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.436191Z","id":"80570a26cbc6b120ce9bd501fe2e6202a97b0d2f3aa8e1becb2cf171aa5e2258","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fdf9020d","summary":"Fixed in fdf9020d: FsContent::read_file answers None, and write_version and copy_version refuse invalid_path before writing, for a path publish::check_path refuses. cargo test -p clax-core content::fs paths_that_leave_the_version_read_nothing_and_write_nothing: passes (failed before: read_file(\"../index.html\") read the version's index.html); clax-core: 906 passed.","supersedes":"27e7b8764246d79c9e5d43c91688dc2d3b2efa693eaa4ff13ff5c0caeef56008","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.444894Z","id":"1b4612855fa9bd50f78a5d3f188714b3dbe9f92bea8366ca6c134c8b3d79f689","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fdf9020d","summary":"Fixed in fdf9020d: local_file and local_clip answer a path only when its file is there. cargo test -p clax-core local_paths_name_only_files_that_are_there: passes (failed before on a file never written).","supersedes":"666847316c6b86150e8ec4a1ac226b18f5b63f3f9cc48d1bb639af8b644d4760","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.941578Z","id":"20996c0b896add5776bff11f794ec8a6799b4ce8e035d1e2a5505219bcf8a0ea","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e7d20b64d05cd549b4d5565ba500faaad11c258626b4bb60fdd26ac4f5aa70e9","span":{"start":{"line":708},"end":{"line":723},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"Since 5d7572d1 the server awaits async twins inline on its request task when the store is on one connection (Store::call_async, store/exec.rs:910), so a lock taken by a future on one tokio worker and resumed on another can now happen natively, but only on a store opened with Store::open_on on a multi-threaded runtime (tests: TestServer::spawn_on_one_connection, CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred). The daemon pool still drives every content job through Store::block_on on a store worker, where the holder thread is exact; a Durable Object has one thread.","supersedes":"d9cbf4fadadc479e8c97d2d14e623d957861308516278267d73e4b9a08b29cdc","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.963894Z","id":"c22335eea66d4baeb20387a342201dad776cb39f23d9b1ec6ede023b4c27e715","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks::held records std::thread::current() when the lock is taken, and Store::lock_content refuses (WouldBlock) a synchronous method on the thread recorded. A future polled by a multi-threaded executor that takes the lock on thread A and resumes on B leaves A recorded: a synchronous method on A is refused although it would not deadlock, and one on B waits for a lock its own thread now drives. Neither happens today (the server drives only synchronous methods, on store workers; a Worker has one thread).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":708},"end":{"line":723},"content_hash":"3c0de9a5ea114ce9cb4aa83114f5849753c98781f788a43bf61b3053f2e383c4"},"summary":"A content lock's holder is the thread it was taken on, so a future that moves threads after taking it is misattributed","supersedes":"e7d20b64d05cd549b4d5565ba500faaad11c258626b4bb60fdd26ac4f5aa70e9","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
